  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Group size and spacing, crater edge, rock plates and dust vary; the heave and the hang are fixed so the slam is always telegraphed."
  },
  "director_notes": "Two-handed maul (caster_weapon kind maul: a 66 px haft with a 17 px iron head; caster_blade sits in the head, caster_blade_tip on top of it). The cleave gesture is high at 55% (about 500 ms), hangs, and lands at 820 ms. Two shock rings: a thin bright front on the hit, then a slow dust wall that keeps pace with the rock plates. Splash layout: the struck enemy plus 3-5 round it, knocked back 90 ms per unit outward. Built to try a Mixamo character as the caster: pick it in the viewer's Caster list or open with ?model=<file>."
